# =====================================================================
# Release V174 -- name the third consent state
# =====================================================================
# V173 made Gold.Dim_Patients.Marketing_Consent hold all three states, as
# 'Opted in' / 'Opted out' / NULL. This names the third one 'Never asked'.
#
# WHY IT IS WORTH A RELEASE OF ITS OWN. A NULL is not a category. In a slicer it appears as
# "(Blank)" if it appears at all; in a chart the rows silently drop out rather than showing as
# the largest group, which on tenant 100 is 6,739 of 7,029 active patients -- by far the most
# important thing the field has to say. A reader also has to be TOLD that NULL means "never
# asked" rather than "no", and nobody reads the load procedure. The value says it instead.
#
# ==> THE DATA-QUALITY CHECK HAD TO MOVE IN THE SAME RELEASE. <== PAT_NO_MARKETING_PREF in
# Gold.usp_Load_Aggregate_Data_Quality tested `Marketing_Consent IS NULL`. Once the load writes
# a string, that predicate matches nothing and the check reports a permanent 0 -- which on this
# scorecard is indistinguishable from a practice with nothing to fix. Shipping the rename alone
# would have silently switched the check off. It is now
# `ISNULL(Marketing_Consent, 'Never asked') = 'Never asked'`, which is correct against both the
# old and the new representation, so the order the two procedures run in cannot make it lie.
#
# COLLATION. The warehouse is Latin1_General_100_BIN2_UTF8 -- binary, case-sensitive -- so the
# literal in the check must match the literal in the load exactly, character for character.
# Both are written as 'Never asked'. Changing the casing in one place only would break the
# check silently, in the same way IS NULL would have.
#
# STILL NO CONSUMERS. PBI/ and Web/ reference Marketing_Consent nowhere, so the values remain
# free to change. This is the last moment that is true for free.
#
# Gold.usp_Load_Dim_Patients is hash-gated and Marketing_Consent sits in both sides of the hash
# by column name, so every row re-hashes and updates on the next run. No Silver change, no
# Bronze clear.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V174__name_the_never_asked_consent_state.manifest
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Dim_Patients.StoredProcedure.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Aggregate_Data_Quality.StoredProcedure.sql

EXEC     DECLARE @i BIGINT,@u BIGINT,@d BIGINT; EXEC Gold.usp_Load_Dim_Patients @Mode='PROD',@Run_Inserts=@i OUT,@Run_Updates=@u OUT,@Run_Deletes=@d OUT;
EXEC     DECLARE @i BIGINT,@u BIGINT,@d BIGINT; EXEC Gold.usp_Load_Aggregate_Data_Quality @Mode='PROD',@Run_Inserts=@i OUT,@Run_Updates=@u OUT,@Run_Deletes=@d OUT;

TEST
